        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: దిగులు",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "దిగులు — digulu — \"gloom; low spirits; worry\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "అమ్మ దూరంగా ఉంటే నాకు దిగులుగా ఉంటుంది. amma dūraṅgā uṇṭē nāku digulugā uṇṭundi. When mum is far away, I feel low."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Said with the dative: నాకు దిగులుగా ఉంది, I feel low."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "దిగులు (digulu) is native Dravidian: DEDR 3202 lists Telugu digulu, \"fear, alarm\", beside Tamil tikil, \"fright, terror\". In everyday Telugu the fear has softened into a heavy, anxious sadness."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
