        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: చింతించు",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "చింతించు — cintiñcu — \"to worry; to regret\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "నాన్న డబ్బు గురించి చాలా చింతించాడు. nānna ḍabbu guriñci cālā cintiñcāḍu. Dad worried a lot about money."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): చింతించాను, cintiñcānu."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What you worry about takes గురించి. The noun is చింత, worry or care."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "చింతించు (cintiñcu) is borrowed from Sanskrit cintayati, \"thinks; cares for\" (CDIAL 4815), and takes the Telugu ending -ఇంచు, which turns a Sanskrit stem into a verb. Thinking too much about a thing becomes worrying about it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
