          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "కలవరపడు — kalavarapaḍu — \"to be agitated; to be upset\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ఆ వార్త విని అమ్మ కలవరపడింది. ā vārta vini amma kalavarapaḍindi. Hearing that news, mum was upset."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): కలవరపడ్డాను, kalavarapaḍḍānu."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The noun is కలవరం, confusion of mind. A noun of feeling + -పడు means to feel it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "కలవరపడు (kalavarapaḍu) is native Dravidian: DEDR 1306 lists Telugu kalavaramu, \"confusion, anxiety\", and kalavara-paḍu, \"to be confused\", beside Tamil kalavaram, \"perturbation\". The second part is the native verb paḍu, \"to feel, to suffer\" (DEDR 3853)."
            }
          ]
        },
