          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ఆత్రుత — ātruta — \"eagerness; impatience\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ఫలితాల కోసం విద్యార్థులు ఆత్రుతగా ఎదురుచూశారు. phalitāla kōsaṁ vidyārthulu ātrutagā edurucūśāru. The students waited eagerly for the results."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Mostly as an adverb: ఆత్రుతగా, eagerly, impatiently."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ఆత్రుత (ātruta) is usually traced to Sanskrit ātura, \"suffering, troubled in body or mind\" (Monier-Williams), with an abstract ending. The restless feeling became eager impatience."
            }
          ]
        },
